# What `git archive` leaves out of the source release.
#
# The tarball is for building, testing and packaging the software, so what goes
# is what serves none of those.  Note what stays and is easy to think optional:
# `README.md', `docs/manual.org' and `config.example.json' are pulled into the
# test binary by `include_str!', and `.github/' is read by an elisp test that
# checks the release asset names against the workflow that publishes them.
# Drop any of the four and `make test' fails on a fresh unpack.

# Screenshots.  Half the archive, and nothing builds or tests from them.
docs/images/ export-ignore

# The vendored ReadTheOrg theme, which only `make html' uses -- and that target
# installs htmlize from MELPA as it runs, so it never worked offline from a
# tarball to begin with.  Leaving it out also keeps the archive MIT throughout:
# this is the one GPL-3 thing in the tree.
docs/org-html-themes/ export-ignore
